I fixed #1172 and committed it as c157098b. config get and config show now say the same thing the run does about a config value it ignores. Format, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test all pass.

What changed for the user (I checked with the built binary in a temp HOME, pointing at a dead 127.0.0.1 address):
```
$ yoyo config get model
  model is not set: .yoyo.toml has model = "", which yoyo reads as unset (using default)
$ yoyo config show
  model     =   (read as unset; using default)
```
yoyo -p hi still runs the default gpt-6-sol and fails with connection refused on 127.0.0.1, which matches what config get now reports.

How it works: whether an empty value counts as "unset" depends on the key, so there's no single rule to share. The new run_reads_as_unset(key, value) in src/commands_config_get.rs asks each key's own run-time reader whether the value is treated as missing. For model, I moved the run's trim-and-check-empty rule out of cli.rs into config_value::named_model, and both the run and config get now call it.

Which keys treat `""` as unset (checked against all 21 entries in SETTABLE_KEYS): 19 do. The two that don't are shown as before:
• `provider = ""` is refused as an unknown provider when no base_url is set.
• `thinking = ""` prints a warning and runs at medium.

A test goes through the whole key list and fails if a new key isn't classified.

Things to know:
• Broader than empty values: an unrecognised boolean ("maybe") or a number that doesn't parse is now also reported as unset, because the run ignores those too. A boolean set to its default value, like auto_continue = "true", still shows as set.
• Positive control: with the new check disabled, both table tests failed by name. After restoring it, all 16 tests passed and no marker was left in the file.
• New issue #1194: config get max_tokens and config show print max_tokens = ***, because the secret-key check masks any key name containing "token". My test table ran into it, so that test uses max_turns instead and cites #1194.
• File size: I added config show's marker to commands_config.rs, making it 2026 lines. That's over the 2000-line cap but inside the 50-line grace band, so the size gate warns rather than failing.
• Docs: docs/src/getting-started/installation.md now describes the new output.

#1172 had no comments to reconcile. The only user-facing references to it are in the code I changed, and I updated the one test comment that pointed to it.
